        "text": "In the current study, we considered three components of math achievement in middle school that are emphasized in state math standards (e.g., National Governors Assocation Center for Best Practices, 2010) and on college-readiness assessments (ACT, 2022). First, there is a heavy emphasis on algebra and functions knowledge, including knowledge of expressions, equations, inequalities and functions (referred to as algebra for brevity). Second, geometry is a core topic and includes knowledge of shapes and solids, such as congruence and similarity relationships. Third, number and quantity knowledge, especially knowledge of the number system and of fractions, is foundational to math achievement in high school (Siegler et al., 2012). Overall, we expected prior math achievement to predict future math achievement from pre-K through high school. We also expected that students' middle-school math achievement would be a mediator of the relation between pre-K math achievement and end-of-high-school math achievement.",
