      "snippet": {
        "text": "The use of artificial intelligence (AI) in education has gained significant attention in recent years, and one of the promising applications of AI in education is the use of language models for language and content-based instruction. Language models are AI models that can generate highquality text based on a given prompt, and ChatGPT is a language model developed by OpenAI that has shown promising results in generating natural and engaging text. \n\nSeveral studies have explored the potential of chatbots and conversational agents in education, showing that they can provide personalized and immediate feedback to learners and enhance their engagement and motivation (Rai & Sarkar, 2021). ChatGPT, in particular, has the potential to facilitate language and content-based learning by generating responses to learners' inputs and providing feedback on grammar, vocabulary, and pronunciation. \n\nHowever, the integration of AI in education also poses challenges, such as the lack of interpretability and the potential for bias in language models (Dhawan, 2021). Therefore, it is crucial to explore the use of ChatGPT in education carefully and develop effective pedagogical practices that leverage its potential. \n\nSeveral studies have explored the use of chatbots and conversational agents in language learning. For example, Li et al. ( 2021) developed a chatbot that uses natural language processing and deep learning algorithms to provide personalized feedback to learners in Chinese as a second language. The results showed that the chatbot was effective in improving learners' grammar and vocabulary skills. \n\nSimilarly, Thorne et al. ( 2019) developed a conversational agent that used machine learning algorithms to provide feedback on learners' pronunciation in English as a second language. The results showed that the conversational agent was effective in improving learners' pronunciation accuracy and confidence. \n\nHowever, these studies mainly focused on the development of the technology and its effectiveness in improving language skills, rather than the design and implementation of pedagogical practices that effectively leverage the potential of the technology. \n\nTherefore, this research aims to fill this gap by designing activities that effectively use ChatGPT to facilitate language and content-based learning. By identifying the characteristics of effective activities, designing and developing a set of activities, and evaluating their effectiveness in a classroom setting, the research can provide valuable insights into the development of pedagogical practices that leverage the potential of ChatGPT in teaching and learning.",
