        }
      },
      "snippet": {
        "text": "At a general level, it has been claimed that ChatGPT is a \"revolutionary tool for teaching and learning mathematics\" (Wardat et al., 2023). Wardat et al. study's aim was to investigate the perspective of various stakeholders (e.g., students, educators) on the use of artificial intelligence in teaching mathematics, in particular after ChatGPT had been launched. Interview results showed that ChatGPT was recognized for its \"improved mathematics capabilities and ability to increase educational success by providing users with basic knowledge of mathematics and various topics\" (p. 1). Similarly, investigating which Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems can be beneficial to mathematics education, Mohamed et al. (2022) claim, based on a systematic review of the literature (mainly studies from the USA and Mexico between the years 2017 and 2021), that AI \"provides a chance to help teachers and students to solve and improve teaching and learning performances\" (p. 1). They offered an overview of AI in mathematics teaching and learning for students at all levels of education. \n\nThe findings of the survey suggested that (for the samples studied) the main areas where an AI approach was used in mathematics education were through robotics (e.g., in LEGO robotics), intelligent tutoring systems (ITS), intelligent instructional tools (based on machine learning models), teachable agents (e.g., for learning number sense), and autonomous agents that solve mathematics puzzles through natural language processing (NLP), for example. In terms of current applications of AI in mathematics education, albeit aimed at researchers in AI and Machine Learning, van Vaerenbergh and Pérez-Suay (2022) provided an overview of the different AI systems that are being used in contemporary digital tools for mathematics education, such as AI-based calculators and ITS. Moreover, they shed some light on the specific technologies that were being used in mathematics educational applications.",
